Z||000000||SN1PERVII||12-06-1999||12:13 AM|||| Hey i was checking the want adds today and i saw an '88 four banger for 2000. I realy would rather get a six but i would also like the upgraded supension. would it be poible to put a six in the fours frame? would it be cost efective to do this. or should i settle for an older model with a six and a mor reasonable price. are therre any upgrades i can do to a '85-'87 suspinsion to bring it up to par with an '88? or am i really just over estimating the signifigance of it? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||12-06-1999||09:57 AM||||SCCA FIERO has an 88 Coupe into which he installed a V6 from an 86 SE.  Search through the old Tech threads and you'll find his posts about it.  It seemed hard, but much easier than, say, a 3800 swap.<P>There really is a significant difference between the 88's and previous suspension and brakes.  The 88 brakes are fantastic and the car deals much better with rough pavement and doesn't bounce all over the place.  <P>Be aware that the 88 Coupe does not have a rear sway bar like the Formula and GT do.  Also, when I bought my 88 Coupe, the rear springs were shot and saggy, and I had to replace them with GT springs.  Something to watch out for.||||reg||1
